  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Solve these inequations with quadratics on both sides.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+x-1<x^2+4x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1<x<4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-3x-4&<0\\\\(x+1)(x-4)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-1$ and $4$. The upward-opening parabola is below the $x$-axis between its zeroes. Hence $-1<x<4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+5x+6\\le -x^2+x+12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3\\le x\\le 1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+4x-6&\\le0\\\\x^2+2x-3&\\le0\\\\(x+3)(x-1)&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-3$ and $1$. The upward-opening parabola is on or below the $x$-axis between and including its zeroes. Hence $-3\\le x\\le1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2+4x+3\\ge -x^2+5x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-1$ or $x\\ge\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-x-3&\\ge0\\\\(x+1)(2x-3)&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-1$ and $\\frac32$. The upward-opening parabola is on or above the $x$-axis outside and including its zeroes. Hence $x\\le-1$ or $x\\ge\\frac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$4x^2-7x-2>x^2-2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-\\frac13$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-5x-2&>0\\\\(3x+1)(x-2)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-\\frac13$ and $2$. The upward-opening parabola is above the $x$-axis outside its zeroes. Hence $x<-\\frac13$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
